<p style="text-align: center;">At Carkeek Beach. 9x12, oil and cold wax medium on linen panel. 2016</p>
<p><span style="line-height: 1.42857;">After getting an early start in the studio and putting in a few hours of painting I headed to the beach at Carkeek Park just north of Ballard. There were few clouds in the sky&nbsp;so I was able to make the painting about&nbsp;the value and temperature changes that were happening above the horizon line.</span></p>
<p>The weather was ten degrees warmer than yesterday morning, but still cold enough to cause my hands to freeze - I must get some painting gloves!</p>
